  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 22.14, p. 427. Book: EFL 100, BFL 154.7, NA -0.3183 (F/1.5), GIH 5.0 (HFOV=2.86), PTZ/F 41.35, VL 782.4, infinite conjugate. Wavelengths 0.4416 um as in the book (primary first). Glass: BK7 entered as N-BK7. The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front surface. Single wavelength 0.4416 um (HeCd) as in the book; BK7 has the book's index 1.526 there. Discrepancy with the book: the table as printed (checked against a clear photo; its thicknesses add up to the book's VL) gives an EFL of 73.5 and an image distance of 113.7, not the book's 100 and 154.7. No single sign change or misread digit in a radius or thickness reproduces both, so the table probably has a misprint. The image is left at the printed 154.667.",
